  "notes": [
    "This is a structural triage report, not a linguistic accuracy certification.",
    "Entries without an explicit senses array may still be single-sense words; editorial review must decide whether distinct senses are needed.",
    "Entries with multiple parts of speech but no senses array are a priority for sense separation and POS review.",
    "The baseline has no category assignments; Phase 3 must classify all baseline entries as well as new additions.",
    "One-example entries need a second natural, context-appropriate example; preserve existing examples unless they are inaccurate.",
    "An additional 10 common baseline verbs now have separate, sense-level English definitions, Simplified Chinese translations and contextual examples. This increases the explicit-sense coverage while preserving single-POS classification where appropriate.",
    "All 810 baseline entries now have at least two contextual examples. A final duplicate-example scan found one repeated example in “paradigm”; it was replaced with a distinct context. The remaining example queue is empty.",
    "Two additional high-frequency verbs, “avoid” and “decide”, now have separate sense records for their distinct common meanings.",
    "A further 18 baseline entries now have explicit sense records (38 sense records total), including corrected noun/verb and verb/adjective distinctions for “console” and “express”. The Simplified Chinese definitions for “brief” and “compassionate” were also corrected.",
    "2026-11-25 refresh: parsed the latest feature-branch index.html rather than relying on the earlier stale audit snapshot. Current baseline: 810 unique entries; 282 entries with 617 explicit sense records; 528 entries without explicit sense arrays. All 176 multi-POS entries have sense-level records covering every declared part of speech. All 810 entries have at least two examples. The 528 no-sense entries are single-POS entries and remain individually eligible for future additional-sense enrichment where a distinct common meaning is genuinely useful.",
    "2026-11-25 second refresh: 20 additional high-frequency single-POS baseline entries now have two distinct sense records each (active, adapt, afford, borrow, boundary, confidence, confuse, context, create, curious, decision, depend, difference, discover, discuss, effective, effort, encourage, evidence, expect). This adds 40 sense records with individual Simplified Chinese definitions and contextual examples. Current baseline: 810 unique entries; 302 entries with 657 explicit senses; 508 entries without explicit sense arrays. All 176 multi-POS entries have explicit sense coverage; all 810 entries have at least two general examples."
